  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models with scvi_n200 + multiprofile reach ~0.65, while image-only resnet50 (singleprofile, config_010) is very weak at 0.208. The multiprofile + aggregation strategy was the single largest improvement for RNA (pca: 0.485→0.591; scvi: baseline→0.65). Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether the image modality can benefit from multiprofile aggregation, or whether it is fundamentally uninformative for this task. This experiment (config_011: image_only, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool) is a controlled comparison against config_010, changing only the profile/aggregation strategy while holding the encoder fixed. If image accuracy remains near 0.2, it strongly indicates the image signal is too weak to contribute meaningfully in multimodal fusion, allowing us to deprioritize many multimodal configurations. If it improves, it establishes a better image baseline and justifies investing in multimodal experiments. This is the most informative single experiment before committing budget to complex multimodal fusion, as it isolates one key design variable (profile/aggregation) on the image modality."
}

